## Project Summary

*AI-generated project summary produced by `/write-summary`, for future AI sessions catching up without re-analyzing line-by-line; may be out of date — re-run to refresh.*

### Purpose

Docker-based launcher for pre-made Claude Code agents. Each persona ships a `CLAUDE.md` (`agents/<name>.md`) plus a `.lego` file of default *tags*; all share OAuth credentials, slash commands, skills, and toolchain caches. Instances are persistent named sessions per agent (`<agent>__<session>`); prior conversations resume automatically. Tags come in four kinds, all discovered from the `agents/` file tree — nothing about a tag is hard-coded in the launcher.

### Tech Stack

- Python 3.12+ host launcher; deps (canonical list: `pyproject.toml` `[project]`): `prompt_toolkit` (picker TUI), `python-dotenv` (`engine.conf` parsing), `rich` (markdown previews); stdlib elsewhere (`tomllib` for every launcher-authored config, `urllib` for CDN-range fetches).
- Plain **`docker build` / `docker run`** — no compose. Base image (root `Dockerfile`) = debian:trixie-slim + Claude Code + jq/yq/fd/ripgrep + iptables/sudo ({firewall} prerequisites, inert otherwise); per-layer Dockerfiles live in the tag tree.
- `unittest` suite (~600 tests, <1s: `python3 -m unittest discover -s launch/tests`); `mypy launch/ run.py` (`disallow_untyped_defs` for source; tests exempt) + `ruff check .` both clean. No CI gate.

### The tag system

Four kinds (closed set — classes in `launch/tags/`), members open (folders under `agents/<kind>/`, each with a TOML `tag.info`: `short_description` + `full_description`, `shortname`, optional `[addendum]` (CLAUDE.md section w/ launcher placeholders), kind-specific fields):

| Kind | Punct. | Carries | Members shipped |
|---|---|---|---|
| engine | `( )` | `engine.conf` env budget (model/effort); nested dirs overlay parent conf | default, golem, poet, thinker, researcher, breakthrough |
| profession | `[ ]` | Dockerfile image layer (+`tag.docker` build-args); nesting ⇒ requirement | code, code/web |
| specialty | `{ }` | `warn`, `claude_args`, `workspace_readonly`, `[wants]`; optional hidden `_<name>` image layer in the profession tree; `tag.docker` run config | auto (skip-permissions, wants firewall), firewall (iptables whitelist, run-only), dood (docker socket, `_dood` image layer under code/), read-only (`{ro}` — `/workspace` :ro + claims the hidden `policy/_read-only` fragment denying Write/Edit) |
| policy | `< >` | `policy.json` settings fragment; `stance` colors orange (allow) / blue (deny) / white (demand) | web-research `<+qry>`, no-sudo `<-su>`, no-net `<-net>`, vcs-safe `<-push>`, plan-first `<!plan>`, free-bash `<+bash>` (plus the hidden `_read-only` fragment, owned by the `{ro}` specialty) |

`agents/specialty/combos.info` holds multi-tag warnings (dood+auto). STRICT tree rule: a non-`_` dir in a kind subtree MUST have `tag.info`; `_` dirs are hidden assets (image layers or specialty-claimed policy fragments). `scan_all(AGENTS_DIR)` → `Registry`, fail-loud cross-validation at startup.

