### Architecture

Entry: `python3 run.py [target] [--dry-run] [--refresh-installs] [...claude-args]` → `launch()` (`run.py`):

1. `gather_input` — `scan_all` (fail-loud tree validation) → `migrations.ensure_migrated()` (legacy two-map JSON → `instances.toml`, once) → argparse → `require_docker` → picker (`select_agent(registry)`) if no CLI target. Returns (opts, registry).
2. `resolve_target` — cont: `Instance` from the store (workspace validated); new: workspace → session → tag form (`prompt_tags`, pre-checked from `.lego`) → `Instance` via `resolve_build`.
3. `compute_resume_flag` — `["--continue"]` only if a session JSONL exists.
4. `persist_instance` — the store entry always reflects the last launch (new AND cont).
5. `apply_tags` — stage every `tag.docker` mount, dispatch `_apply_*` handlers ({firewall}'s DNS resolve kicks off here, overlapping the build).
6. `setup_state` — CLAUDE.md install (source `.md` + `addendums.compose(chain)`), settings install (base + policy fragments → `<state>/settings.json`), OAuth touch, env staging, mounts, user extras, optional creds.
7. Banner (per-axis tag lines + red unmet-wants warnings) → `ensure_image(inst)` (base + per-layer `docker build`, PARENT_IMAGE threading, per-layer arg_forward) → `prompt_install_failures(image, …)` → `run_container` (cap_adds/entrypoint/env-forwards from contributions; specialty `claude_args` like {auto}'s skip-permissions; execs `docker run --rm -it --name claude-code_<instance>`).

Key mounts: workspace → `/workspace`; `~/.claude-agents/<instance>/` → `/home/claude/.claude` (rw) with the generated `settings.json` RO-file-mounted over `~/.claude/settings.json` (agent can't relax its policies); shared OAuth files; `custom_commands|custom_skills|settings/*` (ro); caches → `/home/claude/<rel>` ([code]); tag.docker mounts ({firewall} scripts, {dood} socket).

`{firewall}` pipeline (`network.py`): Phase 1 resolves critical Anthropic hosts synchronously → `WHITELIST_ADDRESSES` (forwarded via the tag's `env_forward`). Phase 2 streams the rest (~140 curated + user whitelist) to an updater daemon gated on the container AND `/var/run/init-firewall.done` (racing the init script once killed launches), applying ≤100-rule bursts via one `docker exec`. A refresher re-resolves every 5 min, additive-only. CDN-provider ranges (cloudflare/fastly/github/cloudfront/google) are fetched live and cached 3 days; `*.host` wildcards widen to all provider blocks. Status file `domains_pending_resolve.yml` sits in the state dir for the agent to classify ConnectionRefused.

### Conventions and Patterns

- **Everything launcher-authored is TOML** (`.lego`, `tag.info`, `tag.docker`, `combos.info`, `instances.toml`); policies are `.json` because Claude Code settings are JSON; engine budgets are dotenv `.conf`. `instances.toml` writing uses a small fixed-schema emitter (stdlib has no TOML writer); None values are omitted (TOML has no null).
- **Adding a tag = adding folders/files, no launcher code** (see `.claude_dev_guidelines` "A new tag"). `_apply_<name>` handlers in `tag_handlers.py` only for dynamic host-side work; `test_essential_files` pins which tags have handlers and that data-only tags (web, auto) have none.
- **All disk I/O through `file_access`** (atomic `write_text`), **all paths in `paths.py`**, **all docker CLI calls in `docker_config`**. Retired on-disk formats are known ONLY to `tags/migrations.py`.
- Engine conf: nested engine dirs overlay parent conf key-by-key; valueless `KEY` lines are dropped. `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL` additionally becomes an explicit `--effort` CLI flag (`effort_args` — the env var alone doesn't pin fresh sessions).
- Env layering: Dockerfile `ENV` (baked) → engine conf (per-launch `-e`) → `ContainerEnvKey` `container_emit=True` (always-on `-e`: status line, BASH_ENV, cred tokens) → tag `[build] arg_forward` (build-args, `INSTALL_*` glob) → tag `[run] env_forward` (conditional `-e`: WHITELIST_ADDRESSES).
- Wants vs requires: `requires` (tree-derived) hard-cascade in the form; `[wants]` are advisory — red form/banner warnings only (auto wants firewall).
- One acknowledged import cycle: `docker_config ↔ network` (lazy imports inside the updater worker). `.claude_dev_guidelines` holds the full role/placement/anti-pattern rules — read it before adding code.

### Known Issues

- No CI gate, no lockfile — tracked in `ISSUES.md`.
- `docker build` runs per layer on every launch (no image-exists short-circuit) — a few cache-hit seconds each time.
- `install_latest_md` / `install_settings` overwrite their state-dir files every launch — in-container edits are silently discarded (intentional: launcher owns them).
- `--network=host` on builds — permanent workaround for BuildKit bridge DNS issues.
- Dry-run only: an intermittent `Exception in thread phase2-cascade` line can print at exit (daemon DNS thread reaped at interpreter shutdown; real runs block on the container so it can't occur).

